\newlabel{tab:wavelet}{{12}{24}{Wavelet vs.\ no-wavelet under the perceptual objective (full model, \textbf {full val, $3925$ images}). The wavelet \emph {raises} rFID and LPIPS and lowers PSNR/SSIM --- it did not add clean detail}{table.caption.38}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Code-cluster segmentation across the prior$\times $objective grid.} Columns: original, then Runs A, B (standard prior, MSE), \textbf  {A+, B+, E+} (standard prior, LPIPS+GAN, $\beta =.001/.1/1.0$) and C+, D+ (code-centered prior, LPIPS+GAN). Colour $=$ super-cluster ($k$-means, $K{=}10$) of the codeword assigned to each latent patch; per-column headers give the mean over $60$ val images. Every model finds the coarse figure/ground split (row~2: the parachute against the sky), and none produces object-level segments --- a reconstruction codebook tiles \emph  {appearance}, not objects. \textbf  {E+} is the image-space counterpart of \S  \ref {sec:betaceiling}: the most codewords per image of any run ($212.5$) and simultaneously the \emph  {least} coherent map ($22.4\%$) --- maximal KL pressure buys vocabulary, not structure (row~2, where its parachute region is visibly noisier than C+/D+'s). Regenerate with \texttt  {tools/code\_cluster\_segmentation.py}; statistics in \texttt  {reports/code\_cluster\_seg\_all\_runs.json}.}}{25}{figure.caption.36}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:seg}{{16}{25}{\textbf {Code-cluster segmentation across the prior$\times $objective grid.} Columns: original, then Runs A, B (standard prior, MSE), \textbf {A+, B+, E+} (standard prior, LPIPS+GAN, $\beta =.001/.1/1.0$) and C+, D+ (code-centered prior, LPIPS+GAN). Colour $=$ super-cluster ($k$-means, $K{=}10$) of the codeword assigned to each latent patch; per-column headers give the mean over $60$ val images. Every model finds the coarse figure/ground split (row~2: the parachute against the sky), and none produces object-level segments --- a reconstruction codebook tiles \emph {appearance}, not objects. \textbf {E+} is the image-space counterpart of \S \ref {sec:betaceiling}: the most codewords per image of any run ($212.5$) and simultaneously the \emph {least} coherent map ($22.4\%$) --- maximal KL pressure buys vocabulary, not structure (row~2, where its parachute region is visibly noisier than C+/D+'s). Regenerate with \texttt {tools/code\_cluster\_segmentation.py}; statistics in \texttt {reports/code\_cluster\_seg\_all\_runs.json}}{figure.caption.36}{}}
